1
00:00:01,250 --> 00:00:07,760
Over a century ago, beings that
prey on humans suddenly appeared.

2
00:00:09,010 --> 00:00:14,230
Their absolutely overwhelming strength

3
00:00:14,430 --> 00:00:18,940
quickly pushed humanity to
the brink of extinction.

4
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:27,200
The surviving humans constructed
three walls: Maria, Rose, and Sina,

5
00:00:27,410 --> 00:00:30,740
which brought them a century of peace.

6
00:00:30,950 --> 00:00:32,370
However...

7
00:00:48,340 --> 00:00:53,180
Unknown are the names
of the flowers that have been trampled

8
00:00:53,390 --> 00:00:58,640
Birds have fallen to the earth
and long for the wind

9
00:00:58,850 --> 00:01:03,730
Prayers won't solve anything

10
00:01:03,940 --> 00:01:09,070
Only the will to fight
can change the here and now!

11
00:01:09,280 --> 00:01:14,370
O pigs who laugh at the resolve
to walk over corpses to move forward

12
00:01:14,580 --> 00:01:16,910
Livestock complacency? False prosperity?

13
00:01:17,120 --> 00:01:19,790
Give us the freedom of dying,
starving wolves!

14
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:25,170
The humiliation of being caged
is what triggers us to fight back

15
00:01:25,380 --> 00:01:30,470
We hunters slaughter prey
beyond the castle walls,

16
00:01:30,680 --> 00:01:35,680
consumed with surging bloodlust,

17
00:01:35,890 --> 00:01:42,810
as our crimson bows and arrows
pierce scarlet holes into the twilight

18
00:02:04,979 --> 00:02:09,984
Whereabouts of His Left Arm: The Struggle for Trost, Part 5

19
00:02:11,630 --> 00:02:17,310
The Titan assault on Trost District
resulted in heavy soldier casualties,

20
00:02:17,520 --> 00:02:21,890
owing, in part, to the fact that the elite
Scout Regiment was absent at the time.

21
00:02:23,270 --> 00:02:28,940
They had just left that morning
on an exterior scouting mission.

22
00:02:31,610 --> 00:02:35,530
It's here! The main unit
of the Scout Regiment!

23
00:02:35,740 --> 00:02:39,830
Commander Erwin!
Give those Titans a real thrashing!

24
00:02:40,040 --> 00:02:42,580
Look! It's Captain Levi!

25
00:02:42,790 --> 00:02:45,880
They say he's as mighty
as an entire brigade!

26
00:02:46,090 --> 00:02:48,670
Ugh. Talk about annoying...

27
00:02:48,880 --> 00:02:55,470
If their looks of envy catch sight
of how fussy you are, it'll crush them.

28
00:03:00,890 --> 00:03:04,440
Outside await the Titans...!

29
00:03:04,650 --> 00:03:07,940
I wonder what kind we'll see this time!

30
00:03:08,150 --> 00:03:12,570
I hope we find some
Abnormals! That'd be great!

31
00:03:12,780 --> 00:03:15,070
I'd say there's already an
Abnormal right here.

32
00:03:15,280 --> 00:03:17,450
Huh?! Where?!

33
00:03:18,870 --> 00:03:20,290
Here.

34
00:03:20,490 --> 00:03:21,910
Move out!

35
00:03:24,040 --> 00:03:28,960
Exterior scouting and establishing
bases for expansion...

36
00:03:29,170 --> 00:03:31,760
Entrusted with these duties,

37
00:03:31,960 --> 00:03:35,010
the Scout Regiment stands at
the apex of humankind's knowledge.

38
00:03:35,220 --> 00:03:37,180
Survival rates
have increased dramatically

39
00:03:37,390 --> 00:03:40,640
thanks to the resourcefulness
of some members,

40
00:03:40,850 --> 00:03:45,060
but excursions into
Titan territory still always result

41
00:03:45,270 --> 00:03:48,940
in casualties exceeding 30%.

42
00:03:49,150 --> 00:03:55,610
That's simply how overwhelmingly powerful
the Titans are compared to humans.

43
00:03:55,820 --> 00:03:59,740
Just you watch...!

44
00:03:59,950 --> 00:04:03,000
Humanity is...

45
00:04:03,200 --> 00:04:05,500
...going to destroy you all!

46
00:04:05,710 --> 00:04:07,540
The last ones standing...

47
00:04:07,750 --> 00:04:09,590
...will be us!

48
00:04:14,550 --> 00:04:17,640
Just you wait...

49
00:04:18,720 --> 00:04:21,140
Captain Levi is gonna...!

50
00:04:34,230 --> 00:04:36,320
One on the right...

51
00:04:36,530 --> 00:04:37,990
Two on the left...

52
00:04:38,200 --> 00:04:40,870
Captain! I've gathered reinforcements!

53
00:04:41,080 --> 00:04:43,990
Petra. Tend to the soldier below.

54
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:46,410
The rest of you, take the one on the right.

55
00:04:46,620 --> 00:04:48,920
I'll handle the ones on the left.

56
00:04:49,120 --> 00:04:50,750
Captain!

57
00:04:55,340 --> 00:04:57,340
Yahoo!

58
00:05:00,340 --> 00:05:02,180
It's okay!

59
00:05:02,390 --> 00:05:05,890
I won't hurt you! I promise!

60
00:05:09,690 --> 00:05:10,770
Nice try!

61
00:05:10,980 --> 00:05:12,310
Now it's my turn!

62
00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:14,530
Hiyaah!

63
00:05:16,820 --> 00:05:19,660
See? That didn't hurt.

64
00:05:20,780 --> 00:05:23,080
Every single one of you...

65
00:05:26,580 --> 00:05:29,210
...looks as funny as hell...

66
00:05:42,930 --> 00:05:43,970
Whoops.

67
00:05:44,180 --> 00:05:46,020
Just simmer down.

68
00:05:46,600 --> 00:05:49,390
Otherwise, I might have trouble...

69
00:05:50,560 --> 00:05:53,400
...shaving your flesh cleanly off.

70
00:06:03,450 --> 00:06:05,490
How filthy...

71
00:06:14,590 --> 00:06:15,750
Captain!

72
00:06:15,960 --> 00:06:19,010
I can't get the bleeding to stop...!

73
00:06:22,220 --> 00:06:24,640
Cap... tain...

74
00:06:28,770 --> 00:06:30,180
Yes?

75
00:06:31,350 --> 00:06:33,980
W-Was I...

76
00:06:34,190 --> 00:06:40,490
...helpful to humanity... at all...?

77
00:06:40,690 --> 00:06:45,120
Am I... going to die... without
having been...

78
00:06:45,320 --> 00:06:47,450
...any help at all...?

79
00:06:51,080 --> 00:06:53,830
You achieved many great things.

80
00:06:54,040 --> 00:06:57,500
And... you'll continue to.

81
00:06:57,710 --> 00:07:03,220
The resolve you leave behind
will give me strength.

82
00:07:03,430 --> 00:07:04,930
I promise you.

83
00:07:05,140 --> 00:07:10,890
I will put an end to the Titans, without fail!

84
00:07:11,100 --> 00:07:13,100
Captain...

85
00:07:13,310 --> 00:07:15,730
He's already...

86
00:07:20,150 --> 00:07:23,570
Did he hear it all?

87
00:07:23,780 --> 00:07:27,120
Yes. I'm sure he heard you.

88
00:07:27,320 --> 00:07:32,620
He's resting with a
look of relief on his face...

89
00:07:34,290 --> 00:07:36,500
That's good, then.

90
00:07:37,330 --> 00:07:38,750
Levi!

91
00:07:39,920 --> 00:07:41,210
We're pulling out!

92
00:07:41,420 --> 00:07:43,300
- Huh?
- Pulling out?

93
00:07:43,510 --> 00:07:46,010
But we can still go further!

94
00:07:46,220 --> 00:07:47,890
My men will have died for nothing!

95
00:07:48,100 --> 00:07:52,640
A swarm of Titans has begun
moving northward, toward the city.

96
00:07:54,640 --> 00:07:56,690
This is just like five years ago.

97
00:07:56,900 --> 00:07:58,690
Somethings happening in town.

98
00:07:58,900 --> 00:08:02,860
It's possible the Wall's been destroyed.

99
00:08:04,570 --> 00:08:05,990
Damn...

100
00:08:09,580 --> 00:08:10,990
Damn...

101
00:08:40,900 --> 00:08:44,990
This... This can't be happening...!

102
00:08:45,190 --> 00:08:48,240
We're nothing like
we were five years ago...

103
00:08:48,450 --> 00:08:50,410
We trained so hard...

104
00:08:50,620 --> 00:08:52,700
We studied so hard...

105
00:08:54,540 --> 00:08:57,370
To beat these things...

106
00:08:57,580 --> 00:09:00,790
To survive against them...

107
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:02,750
Hot...

108
00:09:02,960 --> 00:09:05,050
It's hot...

109
00:09:05,260 --> 00:09:07,260
Help me...

110
00:09:07,470 --> 00:09:08,880
Mom...

111
00:09:09,970 --> 00:09:11,390
Mom...

112
00:09:14,100 --> 00:09:15,520
Mom...

113
00:09:19,560 --> 00:09:20,980
Mom...

114
00:09:23,690 --> 00:09:26,780
Help me...

115
00:09:26,990 --> 00:09:28,990
How did things turn out this way?

116
00:09:29,200 --> 00:09:32,740
Why has everything been taken from us?

117
00:09:32,950 --> 00:09:34,370
Our lives...

118
00:09:34,580 --> 00:09:36,450
Our dreams...

119
00:09:37,870 --> 00:09:39,290
Why?!

120
00:09:45,880 --> 00:09:47,210
Damn it!

121
00:09:47,420 --> 00:09:49,510
Damn it! Damn it!

122
00:09:50,130 --> 00:09:52,640
I refuse to give up!

123
00:09:52,840 --> 00:09:57,720
I'll drive them all out!
Every last one!

124
00:09:58,350 --> 00:10:02,060
By my own hand!

125
00:10:56,370 --> 00:10:59,660
I'll drive you out...

126
00:10:59,870 --> 00:11:01,710
...from this world...

127
00:11:05,960 --> 00:11:08,960
Every last one of you...!

128
00:11:14,970 --> 00:11:16,180
More...

129
00:11:16,970 --> 00:11:18,390
More!

130
00:11:18,970 --> 00:11:20,640
Kill more!

131
00:11:20,850 --> 00:11:22,770
I want to kill!

132
00:11:25,520 --> 00:11:29,110
More... I'm going to...

133
00:11:29,320 --> 00:11:31,690
...kill more of you...

134
00:11:35,450 --> 00:11:36,870
Eren?

135
00:11:50,090 --> 00:11:51,510
Eren!

136
00:11:52,380 --> 00:11:54,880
Eren! Can you move on your own?!

137
00:11:55,090 --> 00:11:56,510
Are you yourself?!

138
00:11:56,720 --> 00:11:58,970
Tell them everything you know!

139
00:11:59,180 --> 00:12:01,810
I'm sure they'll understand!

140
00:12:02,560 --> 00:12:04,060
- Armin?!
- Did you hear him?!

141
00:12:04,270 --> 00:12:06,190
He said he's gonna kill us!

142
00:12:06,400 --> 00:12:08,520
Yeah, I heard it too.

143
00:12:08,730 --> 00:12:12,030
He's planning on eating us!

144
00:12:12,230 --> 00:12:15,360
What are they talking about?

145
00:12:15,570 --> 00:12:19,990
Are they pointing those swords at us?!

146
00:12:20,200 --> 00:12:24,000
They're meant for
taking out Titans, though!

147
00:12:24,200 --> 00:12:27,620
Why are they looking at me like that?

148
00:12:28,750 --> 00:12:32,170
What's going on here?!

149
00:12:48,190 --> 00:12:52,020
You cadets will prep up and
remain on standby!

150
00:12:53,280 --> 00:13:00,410
...And that's how we got ahold
of some gas and got out of Trost.

151
00:13:00,620 --> 00:13:02,450
You went through all that?

152
00:13:02,660 --> 00:13:03,870
I'm sorry.

153
00:13:04,080 --> 00:13:07,790
We kept volunteering
to help supply you guys, but...

154
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:11,710
We'd even managed
to secure some gas, too.

155
00:13:11,920 --> 00:13:17,170
D-Does that mean
everyone who isn't here is...?

156
00:13:17,380 --> 00:13:18,800
Yeah...

157
00:13:20,390 --> 00:13:22,350
Even Mikasa?

158
00:13:22,550 --> 00:13:27,730
No, I'm pretty sure she came after us,
with Jean and the rest...

159
00:13:27,930 --> 00:13:32,020
Jean. Don't tell me
Mikasa got hurt or something?

160
00:13:33,190 --> 00:13:36,280
Hey. What's wrong?

161
00:13:41,110 --> 00:13:45,620
I can't tell you. We've been
slapped with a confidentiality order.

162
00:13:45,830 --> 00:13:48,540
- A confidentiality order?
- That's crazy.

163
00:13:48,750 --> 00:13:52,380
There's no way it's staying
under wraps, though.

164
00:13:52,580 --> 00:13:56,050
The news is gonna spread
across mankind like wildfire.

165
00:13:57,300 --> 00:14:01,050
Assuming mankind
lasts long enough, anyway.

166
00:14:03,140 --> 00:14:05,100
That's pretty smart of the Corps of Engineers,

167
00:14:05,310 --> 00:14:09,060
using the Titans themselves as
a defensive wall of flesh.

168
00:14:09,270 --> 00:14:12,940
But we can't afford to let our guard down.

169
00:14:13,150 --> 00:14:14,940
After all, we're standing on the cliff's edge...

170
00:14:15,150 --> 00:14:19,490
the front lines in the battle
between humanity and the Titans.

171
00:14:19,690 --> 00:14:21,110
What's the matter?

172
00:14:21,320 --> 00:14:24,820
Oh, no, nothing's wrong with our mission.

173
00:14:25,030 --> 00:14:29,160
I'm just worried about my
friends assigned to the vanguard...

174
00:14:29,370 --> 00:14:32,960
I just saw a messenger headed
for HQ with a pale look on his face...

175
00:14:33,170 --> 00:14:34,130
Yeah.

176
00:14:34,330 --> 00:14:36,710
But our only focus should
be on fending them off,

177
00:14:36,920 --> 00:14:39,210
just as we were originally trained.

178
00:14:40,510 --> 00:14:44,840
I heard you helped three
children escape five years ago

179
00:14:45,050 --> 00:14:47,510
and that they're cadets now.

180
00:14:47,720 --> 00:14:49,430
Were they part of the vanguard too?

181
00:14:49,640 --> 00:14:51,060
Yes...

182
00:14:51,770 --> 00:14:54,600
I apologize. I shouldn't have brought it up.

183
00:14:54,810 --> 00:14:56,570
They're fine.

184
00:14:56,770 --> 00:14:58,280
They're tough kids.

185
00:14:58,480 --> 00:15:01,280
They each have what it takes to survive.

186
00:15:01,490 --> 00:15:03,950
One's a proficient fighter.

187
00:15:04,160 --> 00:15:06,530
Another has immense inner strength.

188
00:15:06,740 --> 00:15:11,000
And the other is extremely intelligent.

189
00:15:11,200 --> 00:15:14,500
They're all right. They're alive for sure.

190
00:15:15,580 --> 00:15:19,920
Cadets Jaeger, Ackermann, and Arlelt!

191
00:15:20,130 --> 00:15:23,680
What you've committed is an act of treason!

192
00:15:23,880 --> 00:15:26,930
Whether you live or die depends on you!

193
00:15:27,140 --> 00:15:28,260
Huh?

194
00:15:28,470 --> 00:15:32,060
Should you try anything funny or
attempt to move from where you are,

195
00:15:32,270 --> 00:15:36,230
we'll blast you to bits immediately
and without hesitation!

196
00:15:36,440 --> 00:15:37,520
Huh?

197
00:15:37,730 --> 00:15:39,650
This is a direct question!

198
00:15:39,860 --> 00:15:42,490
What are you really?!

199
00:15:42,690 --> 00:15:45,780
Human?! Or Titan?!

200
00:15:45,990 --> 00:15:50,040
Wh-What kind of question is that?

201
00:15:50,240 --> 00:15:52,580
What's with that look?!

202
00:15:52,790 --> 00:15:56,920
It's almost like they're looking
at some kind of monster...

203
00:15:57,130 --> 00:15:59,210
Is that what they think of me?!

204
00:15:59,420 --> 00:16:03,590
L-I don't understand the question, Sir!

205
00:16:03,800 --> 00:16:05,760
Playing innocent, huh?!

206
00:16:05,970 --> 00:16:08,760
Just try that again, monster!

207
00:16:08,970 --> 00:16:10,680
We'll blast you into
pieces in the blink of an eye,

208
00:16:10,890 --> 00:16:14,640
before you can reveal your true form!

209
00:16:14,850 --> 00:16:16,020
True form?!

210
00:16:16,230 --> 00:16:19,020
Scores of people witnessed the moment

211
00:16:19,230 --> 00:16:24,190
that you appeared from the body of a Titan!

212
00:16:24,400 --> 00:16:31,620
We've allowed an unknown being--
you--to infiltrate Wall Rose!

213
00:16:31,830 --> 00:16:36,080
Even if you are a member of
the Cadets as sanctioned by the king,

214
00:16:36,290 --> 00:16:39,380
it is well within reason for me to
eliminate any risk as quickly as possible!

215
00:16:39,580 --> 00:16:42,340
Of this, I feel certain!

216
00:16:42,550 --> 00:16:46,010
The Armored Titan that took down Wall Maria

217
00:16:46,220 --> 00:16:48,760
could appear at any moment now!

218
00:16:48,970 --> 00:16:53,180
As we speak, the very
survival of humanity is at stake!

219
00:16:53,390 --> 00:16:54,430
Understand?!

220
00:16:54,640 --> 00:16:59,810
We can't afford to waste any
further manpower or time on you!

221
00:17:00,020 --> 00:17:04,780
I will bombard you with
high explosives if I have to!

222
00:17:04,980 --> 00:17:09,490
Indeed, their defiance is obvious.

223
00:17:09,700 --> 00:17:13,030
It's unlikely we'll get any
beneficial information from them.

224
00:17:13,240 --> 00:17:16,960
As you said, this is a
waste of time and manpower.

225
00:17:17,160 --> 00:17:18,040
Sir!

226
00:17:18,250 --> 00:17:19,830
Now is our best chance!

227
00:17:20,040 --> 00:17:23,710
We should destroy him
while he's still in human form!

228
00:17:23,920 --> 00:17:25,920
My specialty...

229
00:17:26,130 --> 00:17:29,800
...is severing flesh.

230
00:17:30,010 --> 00:17:33,680
I'll gladly demonstrate it, if need be.

231
00:17:33,890 --> 00:17:37,270
If anyone wants to experience my technique...

232
00:17:37,480 --> 00:17:42,060
...then please, by all means, step this way.

233
00:17:42,270 --> 00:17:43,480
Sir.

234
00:17:43,690 --> 00:17:48,320
Mikasa Ackermann was assigned to
escort duty with us elite soldiers.

235
00:17:48,530 --> 00:17:51,780
Her prowess is equal to that
of a hundred ordinary soldiers.

236
00:17:51,990 --> 00:17:55,120
Losing her would be a
great setback for humanity.

237
00:17:55,330 --> 00:17:57,790
Hey, Mikasa! Armin!

238
00:17:58,000 --> 00:17:59,080
What is all this?!

239
00:17:59,290 --> 00:18:00,330
Mikasa!

240
00:18:00,540 --> 00:18:02,580
Attacking people won't help!

241
00:18:02,790 --> 00:18:06,590
There's nowhere to run
inside this cramped wall!

242
00:18:06,800 --> 00:18:11,550
I don't care who it is.
I won't let anyone kill Eren.

243
00:18:11,760 --> 00:18:13,550
That's all that matters!

244
00:18:13,760 --> 00:18:15,220
Let's talk this out!

245
00:18:15,430 --> 00:18:18,480
None of them understand the situation!

246
00:18:18,680 --> 00:18:21,770
That's why fear's spreading among them!

247
00:18:21,980 --> 00:18:25,480
Am I the only one who
doesn't think I'm a Titan...?!

248
00:18:25,690 --> 00:18:28,820
Damn! I have no memory of how I got here!

249
00:18:30,360 --> 00:18:34,910
I'm too weak to stand, and I could
end up dead if I say the wrong thing...

250
00:18:35,120 --> 00:18:37,080
Being killed by humans?

251
00:18:37,290 --> 00:18:39,160
That's insane...!

252
00:18:40,540 --> 00:18:46,630
What is this about me coming out
of a Titan's body, anyway?!

253
00:18:46,840 --> 00:18:49,550
What the hell are they talking about?!
How is that possible?!

254
00:18:49,760 --> 00:18:52,470
Does that mean that wasn't a dream?!

255
00:18:53,640 --> 00:18:55,350
If that's the case...

256
00:18:55,550 --> 00:18:59,430
...that means I grew an
arm where my sleeve is gone!

257
00:18:59,640 --> 00:19:02,640
That makes me practically like a Titan!

258
00:19:02,850 --> 00:19:05,060
That's impossible...

259
00:19:05,270 --> 00:19:06,940
How could I...?

260
00:19:07,150 --> 00:19:07,650
How?!

261
00:19:07,860 --> 00:19:09,440
I'll ask one more time!

262
00:19:09,650 --> 00:19:12,240
What are you really?!

263
00:19:14,950 --> 00:19:17,700
I can't answer this wrong...

264
00:19:17,910 --> 00:19:21,120
I won't be the only one who'll die...

265
00:19:21,330 --> 00:19:25,500
Yeah, I've always been...

266
00:19:25,710 --> 00:19:28,750
...the same as you!

267
00:19:28,960 --> 00:19:30,590
I'm human!

268
00:19:40,680 --> 00:19:42,640
I see...

269
00:19:42,850 --> 00:19:45,770
Don't take this personally.

270
00:19:47,230 --> 00:19:49,570
This is just how it has to be.

271
00:19:49,770 --> 00:19:54,030
Because no one can prove...

272
00:19:54,240 --> 00:19:57,620
...that they aren't a monster.

273
00:20:00,030 --> 00:20:01,370
Eren! Armin!

274
00:20:01,580 --> 00:20:02,660
Head up the wall!

275
00:20:02,870 --> 00:20:04,290
Stop!

276
00:20:11,050 --> 00:20:12,460
Eren.

277
00:20:13,840 --> 00:20:16,720
When I get back,
I'll show you the basement

278
00:20:16,930 --> 00:20:19,430
that I've kept secret all this time.

279
00:20:21,560 --> 00:20:25,940
Keep this key on you at all times.

280
00:20:26,140 --> 00:20:30,480
And every time you see it, remember.

281
00:20:30,690 --> 00:20:34,070
Remember that you
must visit that basement!

282
00:20:36,610 --> 00:20:41,080
This injection will
make you forget all of this,

283
00:20:41,280 --> 00:20:45,410
so there's no use explaining now.

284
00:20:45,620 --> 00:20:46,620
Listen.

285
00:20:46,830 --> 00:20:51,920
You must retake Wall Maria
and reach the basement!

286
00:20:52,130 --> 00:20:57,010
I'm certain this ability
will help when that time comes!

287
00:20:57,220 --> 00:21:01,300
Their memories will tell you how to use it!

288
00:21:01,510 --> 00:21:02,930
Eren!

289
00:21:04,850 --> 00:21:08,980
You'll understand the truth someday,
if you visit the basement!

290
00:21:09,190 --> 00:21:11,650
It will be a harsh, painful journey...

291
00:21:11,860 --> 00:21:13,860
...but you must reach it!

292
00:21:18,110 --> 00:21:21,740
If you want to save
Mikasa, Armin, and everyone else...

293
00:21:21,950 --> 00:21:26,790
...you must learn to control this ability!

294
00:21:52,480 --> 00:21:54,480
Did we get him?

295
00:22:06,200 --> 00:22:08,040
This can't be...

296
00:22:36,400 --> 00:22:41,320
Your dreams are where your heart is

297
00:22:41,530 --> 00:22:47,580
They're more fragile than life itself

298
00:22:47,790 --> 00:22:52,250
Over and over you cast them aside,
only to find more

299
00:22:52,460 --> 00:22:58,920
Now, rest in peace

300
00:22:59,130 --> 00:23:10,270
Pounding impulses defile the things we wish for

301
00:23:10,480 --> 00:23:20,530
and the more we forget
the more we remember again

302
00:23:20,740 --> 00:23:26,490
In this beautiful, cruel world

303
00:23:26,700 --> 00:23:31,660
all I can do is ask why we're still alive

304
00:23:31,870 --> 00:23:37,380
Oh, with our strength--and our weakness--

305
00:23:37,590 --> 00:23:43,050
what are we going to protect if there's no sense

306
00:23:43,260 --> 00:23:46,680
to anything anymore?

307
00:23:53,640 --> 00:23:59,730
"Eren isn't humanity's enemy,"
Armin desperately pleads.

308
00:23:59,940 --> 00:24:03,490
But the Garrison Regiment,
consumed by fear and abandoning all logic,

309
00:24:03,690 --> 00:24:05,380
makes the decision to execute Eren.

310
00:24:05,380 --> 00:24:06,990
Response: The Struggle for Trost, Part 6
makes the decision to execute Eren.
